      "justification": "Apply end-tidal CO2 monitoring to confirm endotracheal tube placement if intubated, assess quality of CPR (ETCO2 >10 mmHg target), and serve as prognostic indicator. Sudden rise in ETCO2 may indicate ROSC."
    },
    {
      "action_id": "continue_high_quality_cpr",
      "timestamp_minutes": 30.0,
      "type": "reassess",
      "args": {},
      "justification": "Per AHA ACLS guidelines, high-quality CPR must be maintained continuously during cardiac arrest. This is a required action for any cardiac arrest rhythm."
    },
    {
